//! The `grid-row` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS)
//! [shorthand](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Cascade/Shorthand_properties)
//! property specifies a grid item's size and location within a `grid row` by contributing a line, a
//! span, or nothing (automatic) to its grid placement, thereby specifying the inline-start and
//! inline-end edge of its `grid area`.
//!
//! Initial: grid-row-start: auto; grid-row-end: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: <grid-line> [ / <grid-line> ]?
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-grid-2/#propdef-grid-row
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/grid-row
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

